From 123dbdd025dc149e528fb7b17f5cfd800496458c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:46:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 62/68] vgpu: clear GPU-resident GVA targets natively and avoid
 pre-draw DontCare seed wipes

Clear-only render passes (apply_clear) targeting GVA-backed attachments previously wrote 8-bit UNORM texels directly to guest memory without clearing or superseding the Vulkan GPU resident. Subsequent LOAD passes whose seed was elided (gva_resident_authoritative) composited onto stale GPU pixels instead of the cleared surface, and RGBA16Float clear values were quantized to 8-bit UNORM.

Route Vulkan GVA clear-only passes through clear_resident_target + writeback_debt::arm_gva when defer-eligible, and drop any unpaid GVA debt while encoding native-precision float/10-bit/16-bit texels on the synchronous fallback and type-11 mapping clear paths. Also release gpu_only_content when superseding a mapping debt, and run encode_draw_vulkan's CPU clear_seed fallback only when no engine draw returned so real draws never pre-wipe MTLLoadActionDontCare guest pages.
